<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36016" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑνόω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἷς</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>make one, unite,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίαν τὴν πόλιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1261b10
				</span></i>
			&lt;*&gt; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ</span>
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐναντιώτατα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Archyt.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				1.41.2
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ πολυμιγῆ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Herm.
				</span></i>
			 ap. eund.<i><span class="en">
				1.49.3
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἀκούειν τῷ πράττειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.609
				</span></i>
			: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑνοῦν τινὰ τῇ γῇ</span> to
			bury him, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Im.</u>
				2.29
			</span></i>; of <i>mixing</i> drugs, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκριβῶς ἕνωσον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dsc.
					<u>Eup.</u>
					1.13
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				1.31
			</span></i> (
				Pass.
			):—
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.471
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Cleom.
				2.1
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡνῶσθαι τὰ πάντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arr.
					<u>Epict.</u>
					1.14.2
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίμνη . . ἡνωμένη τῇ θαλάσσῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ath.
					7.311d
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ φύσει ἡνωμένα</span>
			<i>things united</i> by nature, <i><span class="en">
				Longin.
				22.3
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἡ.</span>”
				<i>propositions couched in the singular number,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					24.1
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡνωμένοι,</span> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσύντακτοι,</span> of troops, <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>BJ</u>
				3.2.2
			</span></i>; esp. in Philos., <i>unified,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ μὲν ὂν ἀριθμὸς ἡνωμένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plot.
					6.6.9
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἡ.,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ὄν</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Dam.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				20
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				68
			</span></i>, al.</div>
